Given an adjunction between cartesian closed categories
\begin{center}
\begin{tikzcd}[column sep=large]
{\mathord{\mathcal{V}}}\arrow[r, bend left=20, "F"] \arrow[r, phantom, "\bot"] & {\mathord{\mathcal{W}}}\arrow[l, bend left=20, "U"]   \end{tikzcd}
\end{center}
whose left adjoint preserves finite products then if ${\mathord{\mathcal{C}}}$ is co/tensored as a ${\mathord{\mathcal{W}}}$-cat\-e\-gory,  $U_*{\mathord{\mathcal{C}}}$ is co/tensored as ${\mathord{\mathcal{V}}}$-category with the co/tensor of $c \in {\mathord{\mathcal{C}}}$ by $v \in {\mathord{\mathcal{V}}}$ defined by
\[ v \otimes c \coloneq Fv \otimes c \qquad \text{and} \qquad c^v \coloneq c^{Fv}.\]
\end{proposition}

